WEBVTT

00:00:50.135 --> 00:00:53.554
- Ah, Xmas season is upon us.

00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:55.055
Secure the perimeter!

00:00:57.726 --> 00:01:00.019
Razor lights in place?

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.062
- Roger!
- Then, stand back!

00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:10.029
Intruder alert.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:17.419
- Santa's not getting
past that! No way!

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.964
Unless he knocks it down or something.
- Hey, robot.

00:01:19.965 --> 00:01:22.091
- Someone left a card
in your stocking.

00:01:22.092 --> 00:01:23.133
- That's weird.

00:01:23.134 --> 00:01:25.511
Normally, I get mail
delivered to my ass.

00:01:28.682 --> 00:01:31.308
"I know what you
did next Xmas!"?

00:01:31.309 --> 00:01:33.269
Okay... Random!

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.271
- I wonder what
you will have done

00:01:35.272 --> 00:01:37.773
and who could possibly
will have known about it.

00:01:37.774 --> 00:01:40.860
- Eh, I do a lot of stuff. I'm
probably doing something right now.

00:01:44.864 --> 00:01:48.909
- Who's ready for their very
first animated holiday special?

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.244
- Hooray!
- So fun!

00:01:50.245 --> 00:01:51.328
-Whatever.

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:54.624
- Ooh! Wait for me. I love
having other kids around.

00:01:55.292 --> 00:01:59.253
This year's rerun
of There's a Holiday for Everyone

00:01:59.254 --> 00:02:00.713
is brought to you by...

00:02:00.714 --> 00:02:03.132
Mom's Old Fashioned
Blood Remover.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:04.968
Now in oatmeal spice.

00:02:12.726 --> 00:02:15.519
- And that holiday is Xmas.

00:02:18.398 --> 00:02:20.024
Hey,
kids, any chance

00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:21.942
y'all wanna remix
this holiday special,

00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:24.486
and hear the dope story
of Kwanzaabot instead?

00:02:24.487 --> 00:02:27.531
- Or your favorite goofy
golem, Chanukah Zombie?

00:02:27.532 --> 00:02:29.825
- No! Tell us about Santa!

00:02:29.826 --> 00:02:30.909
- Again?

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.245
- Yes! Every year!

00:02:33.246 --> 00:02:34.497
Oy...

00:02:38.668 --> 00:02:41.128
The ancient tradition of Xmas

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:43.714
began in the year 2801,

00:02:43.715 --> 00:02:45.466
when the Friendly Robot Company

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:48.302
developed a high-powered
mechanical Santa

00:02:48.303 --> 00:02:52.557
capable of delivering over
five mega-presents per second.

00:02:58.063 --> 00:02:59.438
Hey...

00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:02.399
They tricked him out
with a pair of carbon-fiber Tims

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.735
and a chrome
naughty-nice sensor.

00:03:04.736 --> 00:03:06.904
So he'd
know who deserved gifts

00:03:06.905 --> 00:03:09.531
and who deserved
brutal punishment.

00:03:09.532 --> 00:03:12.576
- Yo, that might've been the
first mistake right there.

00:03:12.577 --> 00:03:15.037
But on Santa's very first delivery,

00:03:15.038 --> 00:03:18.040
something went
tragically meshuggenah.

00:03:18.041 --> 00:03:21.210
His naughty-nice
sensor malfunctioned.

00:03:21.211 --> 00:03:23.837
Man, that's some
bleeped-up.

00:03:25.715 --> 00:03:27.717
- Yay! Santa's here!

00:03:31.012 --> 00:03:33.472
Oh! Oh my!

00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:35.600
Oh, thank you.

00:03:36.142 --> 00:03:38.018
- I'm sorry, kids.

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:41.272
I never wanted you to
know Santa was real.

00:03:46.653 --> 00:03:49.697
- Yuletide news, everyone!

00:03:49.698 --> 00:03:52.074
I know how to fix Santa!

00:03:53.827 --> 00:03:55.828
I just need to sneak up on him

00:03:55.829 --> 00:03:59.331
and reverse the polarity
of his naughty-nice sensor.

00:03:59.332 --> 00:04:02.835
- But Santa is always on guard
against attacks. Just like me.

00:04:02.836 --> 00:04:04.712
Hii-yah!
- Ow!

00:04:04.713 --> 00:04:06.922
- You'll never be able
to sneak up on him.

00:04:06.923 --> 00:04:08.632
- Not through space, no,

00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:10.676
but through time, probably.

00:04:10.677 --> 00:04:14.638
You see, Santa is only prepared
for an attack from the present.

00:04:14.639 --> 00:04:18.601
So I've been souping
up my old time machine.

00:04:18.602 --> 00:04:19.727
- Where is it?

00:04:19.728 --> 00:04:22.062
- The question is when is it?

00:04:22.063 --> 00:04:24.774
And the answer is right about...

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:27.192
now!

00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:30.487
- It's so amazing.

00:04:30.488 --> 00:04:32.406
I don't even care
that it's on my foot.

00:04:33.408 --> 00:04:37.161
- I've installed a manual
transmission with a reverse gear,

00:04:37.162 --> 00:04:40.873
so it can now go backward
in time as well as forward.

00:04:40.874 --> 00:04:42.708
Hooray...

00:04:42.709 --> 00:04:46.170
- My plan is to back
up to the year 2801,

00:04:46.171 --> 00:04:48.088
when things first went wrong,

00:04:48.089 --> 00:04:50.215
and materialize behind Santa

00:04:50.216 --> 00:04:53.135
as he exits this very fireplace.

00:04:53.136 --> 00:04:55.930
- Did this building
even exist in 2801?

00:04:55.931 --> 00:04:59.391
- Yeah, but back then, it
was some kinda meat market,

00:04:59.392 --> 00:05:02.144
where butchers would hook
up and grind their sausages.

00:05:02.145 --> 00:05:04.104
- Yes, anyway, once there,

00:05:04.105 --> 00:05:06.065
I'll quickly
reverse the polarity

00:05:06.066 --> 00:05:09.902
of Santa's naughty-nice sensor,
then return to the present.

00:05:09.903 --> 00:05:11.946
Problem solved.

00:05:11.947 --> 00:05:15.407
- Um, Professor, isn't it
risky to go back in time

00:05:15.408 --> 00:05:16.784
and change history?

00:05:16.785 --> 00:05:18.243
- Oh my, yes.

00:05:18.244 --> 00:05:20.537
But I'll go alone to
minimize the chance

00:05:20.538 --> 00:05:23.749
of anyone becoming
their own grandfather.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:26.710
- These things happen.
- No, they don't.

00:05:26.711 --> 00:05:30.381
- Next time you see me, Santa
will have been good again!

00:05:30.382 --> 00:05:31.423
Ta-ta!

00:05:34.177 --> 00:05:37.764
Uh, just a couple of
centuries straight backwards.

00:05:40.392 --> 00:05:43.811
Damn it! I backed over Mrs.
McGillicuddy's time cat!

00:05:43.812 --> 00:05:46.814
Clutch, shift, and...

00:05:46.815 --> 00:05:48.941
away we go!

00:06:16.261 --> 00:06:18.305
Ho-ho-hot!

00:06:21.641 --> 00:06:23.727
Cookie.

00:06:34.279 --> 00:06:35.362
Cookie!

00:06:41.036 --> 00:06:42.953
Cookie!

00:06:45.206 --> 00:06:48.667
Just shift into forward and...

00:06:48.668 --> 00:06:49.668
Whoa!

00:06:51.171 --> 00:06:54.923
Oh, bother. I shifted
into reverse by accident.

00:06:54.924 --> 00:06:58.344
I guess I'll have to take her
around by the scenic route.

00:07:04.809 --> 00:07:08.104
Ah, here comes the
Big Backwards Bang.

00:07:09.814 --> 00:07:11.607
Ow! I'm being crushed

00:07:11.608 --> 00:07:14.486
by all the matter that
ever was.

00:07:18.198 --> 00:07:21.075
- And here we are, the future!

00:07:33.088 --> 00:07:34.088
Ee-eye!

00:07:36.383 --> 00:07:38.300
- How'd it go?
- Not a hitch!

00:07:39.761 --> 00:07:41.595
I fixed Santa!

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.724
- It'll be my first happy Xmas

00:07:45.725 --> 00:07:48.686
since I got frozen and
never saw my family again!

00:07:48.687 --> 00:07:50.271
- Now, hold on!

00:07:50.272 --> 00:07:51.772
Xmas isn't for a week.

00:07:51.773 --> 00:07:54.483
Until then, we got
nonstop busy work.

00:07:54.484 --> 00:07:56.735
- Oh fuff. Let's
stop pretending

00:07:56.736 --> 00:07:58.737
we do anything around here.

00:07:58.738 --> 00:08:00.823
Everyone, take the week off,

00:08:00.824 --> 00:08:03.659
and be with your
so-called loved ones.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.119
Really?

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.745
- I forgot I had loved ones!

00:08:06.746 --> 00:08:09.039
It's a human resources miracle!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.959
- Uncle Fry, I hope
you'll join me and Cubert

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.919
at my chalet in the Bronx.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.755
- Wait! My family's
hoping to meet Fry.

00:08:16.756 --> 00:08:18.507
I mean, they met him before,

00:08:18.508 --> 00:08:20.467
but he didn't make
much of an impression.

00:08:20.468 --> 00:08:23.387
- I'll wear out my welcome at
one, and then go to the other.

00:08:30.312 --> 00:08:32.229
- So, Bender...
- No.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:35.274
- You and I are the only
ones with no family.

00:08:35.275 --> 00:08:36.775
Maybe we could...
- No.

00:08:36.776 --> 00:08:39.778
- Hang out?
- Oh. Hang out, you say?

00:08:39.779 --> 00:08:42.032
Let me think that
over for a... No.

00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:44.908
No. Oh, sorry.

00:08:44.909 --> 00:08:46.952
Uh, I thought you
were still talking.

00:09:15.815 --> 00:09:19.778
It's just you
and me, moldy sandwich man.

00:09:26.743 --> 00:09:28.327
- Hello. Calculon acting.

00:09:28.328 --> 00:09:31.121
- Hey, it's me! Your
extremely close friend Bender.

00:09:31.122 --> 00:09:32.122
Wanna hang out?

00:09:32.123 --> 00:09:33.540
- How did you get this number?

00:09:33.541 --> 00:09:36.085
- I didn't! I'm just dialing
every number in order.

00:09:36.086 --> 00:09:37.503
- Keep dialing.

00:09:37.504 --> 00:09:39.213
This nuts bolts!

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.675
- Hey, Bender.
- Yes? I mean no!

00:09:42.676 --> 00:09:44.885
- I brought dumpster nog...

00:09:44.886 --> 00:09:47.596
And not the kind
for kids.

00:09:47.597 --> 00:09:50.100
- Hm. What's in it?
- What's not in it?

00:09:51.142 --> 00:09:52.643
You want nutmeg on that?

00:09:52.644 --> 00:09:54.396
- Nutmeg? Gross!

00:09:57.023 --> 00:09:59.441
Five golden rings!

00:09:59.442 --> 00:10:01.944
Four something something,
three something else

00:10:01.945 --> 00:10:04.488
Two no one cares,
and a partridge

00:10:04.489 --> 00:10:06.156
Drowned in our nog!

00:10:07.158 --> 00:10:09.743
- Whoof! This stuff is strong!

00:10:09.744 --> 00:10:12.371
Hey, how many glasses
have we hadded?

00:10:12.372 --> 00:10:14.707
- None. This is
just from the fumes.

00:10:17.836 --> 00:10:19.336
- Aw, it's not fair!

00:10:19.337 --> 00:10:22.589
Everyone else gets to have
fun with their stupid family.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.925
- My species dies
when we reproduce.

00:10:24.926 --> 00:10:26.927
So if I had a
family, I'd be dead.

00:10:26.928 --> 00:10:29.722
Does anyone even care about that?
- I sure don't.

00:10:29.723 --> 00:10:32.891
- If you ask me, "good"
Santa is ruining Xmas.

00:10:32.892 --> 00:10:36.228
I'd like to give him such
a snipping.

00:10:36.229 --> 00:10:39.982
- Ooh, I'd bend him a new one!
But he's not here right now!

00:10:39.983 --> 00:10:42.359
- But, he has was been here.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:45.070
Every Xmas, he shows
up in the fire hole.

00:10:46.114 --> 00:10:48.657
- We could drunk
drive the time machine

00:10:48.658 --> 00:10:50.993
to last Xmas and kidnap him!

00:10:50.994 --> 00:10:54.330
Then, he won't be able to
deliver presents this Xmas!

00:10:54.331 --> 00:10:57.333
- And our stupid friends'
holiday will be ruined!

00:10:59.127 --> 00:11:01.920
Wait. Is kidnapping
Santa a good idea,

00:11:01.921 --> 00:11:05.299
or does it just seem like a good
idea because we're intoximated?

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:08.135
It's a good idea.

00:11:09.679 --> 00:11:10.930
Whee!

00:11:12.807 --> 00:11:15.643
Set course for last Xmas!

00:11:17.062 --> 00:11:20.731
Jingle bells, Zoidberg
smells just like rotten eggs

00:11:20.732 --> 00:11:23.901
I'm
immortalized in song.

00:11:26.947 --> 00:11:29.323
Cookie?

00:11:30.367 --> 00:11:33.494
- And here we are, last Xmas.

00:11:33.495 --> 00:11:35.079
Get him!

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:38.082
- Bite my glittering
festive ass!

00:11:40.085 --> 00:11:43.087
Unhand me, you
naughty boys!

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:59.812
- Shove him in the
old meat locker!

00:11:59.813 --> 00:12:01.563
- We have an old meat locker?

00:12:01.564 --> 00:12:04.066
Silent night

00:12:04.067 --> 00:12:05.567
Holy night

00:12:11.574 --> 00:12:13.367
- Oh, boy. Hey, boy.

00:12:14.536 --> 00:12:17.831
- Try spreading joy
now, you big Xmas ham.

00:12:20.083 --> 00:12:23.085
- We're geniuses!
- I'm geniuses!

00:12:23.086 --> 00:12:25.379
Do the Bender!
Do the Bender!

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:27.589
Do the Bender!
Do the Bender!

00:12:29.551 --> 00:12:30.759
- You know, Zoidberg,

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:33.095
you're only half as bad
as I thought you were.

00:12:33.096 --> 00:12:35.681
That means a lot.

00:12:35.682 --> 00:12:38.183
Uh-oh.
We woke the meat up.

00:12:44.024 --> 00:12:46.108
- What do we do?
- The time machine!

00:12:46.109 --> 00:12:47.110
Good idea!

00:12:51.114 --> 00:12:54.825
- Get ready to sleep
in heavenly peace!

00:12:56.828 --> 00:12:58.079
Ho, ho...

00:12:58.997 --> 00:13:00.332
Whoa!

00:13:03.835 --> 00:13:07.004
Ooh... Ah...

00:13:07.005 --> 00:13:09.007
Ooh...

00:13:12.135 --> 00:13:15.554
- He's dead. We
killed Santa Claus.

00:13:15.555 --> 00:13:18.807
- Uh... You killed Santy Claus.

00:13:18.808 --> 00:13:21.518
- Uh... Robot?

00:13:30.946 --> 00:13:33.238
- This was supposed to
be a fun kidnapping!

00:13:33.239 --> 00:13:34.490
What do we do now?

00:13:34.491 --> 00:13:37.660
- We gotta get rid of the body.
That's usually pretty fun.

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:42.247
Stroke! Stroke! Stroke! Stroke!

00:13:42.248 --> 00:13:43.249
Stroke!

00:13:44.084 --> 00:13:45.085
- Oops.

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:46.711
Oops.

00:13:47.671 --> 00:13:48.671
Ow!

00:13:50.507 --> 00:13:54.468
- Okay. Now, we just add some
extra weight to sink the corpse.

00:13:56.429 --> 00:13:57.805
- It's not working!

00:13:59.266 --> 00:14:00.308
Still nothing!

00:14:01.309 --> 00:14:03.602
Why! Won't! You! Sink!?

00:14:06.064 --> 00:14:07.064
Ah!

00:14:12.279 --> 00:14:14.363
Hands up, boat bags.

00:14:14.364 --> 00:14:16.282
- What's with the
bloated floater?

00:14:16.283 --> 00:14:18.450
I admit it! We
murd...

00:14:18.451 --> 00:14:21.870
- Uh, just, uh, dumping
some toxic waste, officers.

00:14:21.871 --> 00:14:24.290
- Huh. Guess you gotta
put it somewhere.

00:14:24.291 --> 00:14:26.208
- Carry on, night dumpers.

00:14:32.799 --> 00:14:37.219
- Dwight, it's time to teach you
the Conrad holiday turducken recipe.

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:39.222
Cooked in alphabetical order.

00:14:39.723 --> 00:14:41.015
- Alrighty then.

00:14:41.016 --> 00:14:44.727
We gonna start with the
chicken, then duck, and then...

00:14:44.728 --> 00:14:46.895
Let me see
now. Now the E and the F...

00:14:46.896 --> 00:14:49.565
Husband! We
using flamingo this year?

00:14:49.566 --> 00:14:52.401
- At $20 a pound!?
No, thank you.

00:14:56.781 --> 00:14:58.866
- It's not working!
- Flush harder!

00:14:58.867 --> 00:15:01.910
- I'm flushing as hard as
I can! Got any other ideas,

00:15:01.911 --> 00:15:04.413
Mr.
I'm-So-Great-At-Hiding-Corpses?

00:15:04.414 --> 00:15:07.958
- Well, at least I have
ideas! What do you suggest?

00:15:07.959 --> 00:15:10.669
- Hm... We could
try an acid bath.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.296
- That does sound
relaxing, but...

00:15:12.297 --> 00:15:15.090
- No! We'll dissolve
Santa's body!

00:15:15.091 --> 00:15:17.468
Professor has some acid
upstairs in his lab.

00:15:17.469 --> 00:15:19.095
I'll go fill this trash bag.

00:15:24.267 --> 00:15:26.186
Oops!

00:15:29.856 --> 00:15:32.107
- Remind me, is this
the ground floor?

00:15:34.945 --> 00:15:38.948
- Behold, my family's
traditional Yuletide feast.

00:15:38.949 --> 00:15:41.033
Turdolphin!

00:15:41.034 --> 00:15:44.453
It's fresh turtle cooked
inside a fermented dolphin.

00:15:44.454 --> 00:15:47.581
- Wow. Soon, it's gonna
be barf inside a vomit.

00:15:47.582 --> 00:15:50.626
- Dad. Shh! Keep the
truth to yourself.

00:15:50.627 --> 00:15:52.795
- Which part smells
like whale butt?

00:15:52.796 --> 00:15:54.505
- Ooh, that would be the gravy.

00:15:58.301 --> 00:16:00.094
You ruined everything!

00:16:00.095 --> 00:16:02.263
You're the one who
wanted to kidnap Santa!

00:16:02.264 --> 00:16:04.473
- Oh, yeah? Well,
you enabled me,

00:16:04.474 --> 00:16:08.102
so shut up and keep pushing
him into the meat grinder!

00:16:08.103 --> 00:16:10.605
- Bender, look! It's working!

00:16:11.439 --> 00:16:13.107
Wait. Where's my claw?

00:16:16.111 --> 00:16:18.904
- Gather round,
relatives, as I cook up

00:16:18.905 --> 00:16:21.115
turducken a la Farnsworth

00:16:21.116 --> 00:16:23.534
with this 3D poultry printer.

00:16:23.535 --> 00:16:26.453
- As long as it's got three
dimensions, I'll eat it.

00:16:26.454 --> 00:16:28.664
- We start with liquid chicken.

00:16:31.543 --> 00:16:33.752
Then, some duck filament.

00:16:39.384 --> 00:16:42.344
And finally, a
whole fresh turkey.

00:16:42.345 --> 00:16:44.513
I printed this one out earlier.

00:16:53.398 --> 00:16:56.650
- Oh, man. I need to head out
if I'm gonna make it to Leela's.

00:16:56.651 --> 00:16:59.863
Do you have any skis?
- No, but I can print some.

00:17:05.327 --> 00:17:08.746
- How are we making turducken?
There's nothing in the refrigerator.

00:17:08.747 --> 00:17:11.874
- Eh, that fridge doesn't work.
We use it as a spare bedroom.

00:17:11.875 --> 00:17:14.376
- We serve fresh
turducken, Leela.

00:17:14.377 --> 00:17:17.630
They roam the
sewers in huge flocks.

00:17:20.925 --> 00:17:23.052
- Are they hard to catch?
- Oh, no.

00:17:23.053 --> 00:17:24.845
They crave death.

00:17:28.767 --> 00:17:30.059
- Hey! Sorry I'm late.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:32.102
I got hungry and ate my skis.

00:17:32.103 --> 00:17:33.979
- Fry, you made it!

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:36.315
You remember my
parents and my grandma?

00:17:36.316 --> 00:17:39.109
Ah, yes. The rose of the sewers.

00:17:39.110 --> 00:17:40.110
Mwah!

00:17:40.111 --> 00:17:42.863
- Leela, if you don't marry him,

00:17:42.864 --> 00:17:44.990
I will.

00:17:44.991 --> 00:17:47.451
- So, uh, where's
Bender and Zoidberg?

00:17:47.452 --> 00:17:50.287
- What? I figured they were
with you. Or something.

00:17:50.288 --> 00:17:52.623
They're probably
relaxing by the fire.

00:17:56.211 --> 00:17:59.463
- The only rational
option is to eat Santa.

00:17:59.464 --> 00:18:01.090
Right? Right!?

00:18:01.091 --> 00:18:02.341
- I don't know!

00:18:02.342 --> 00:18:04.927
Oh, this is a
nightmare before Xmas.

00:18:04.928 --> 00:18:06.804
I wish we'd never
become friends!

00:18:06.805 --> 00:18:09.807
- We're not friends!
And we never were!

00:18:11.017 --> 00:18:13.602
- But we danced. And murdered.

00:18:14.688 --> 00:18:17.773
- I'll do the carving. You want
white Christmas or dark Christmas?

00:18:21.111 --> 00:18:23.028
Surprise!

00:18:23.029 --> 00:18:24.531
- Bah humbug!

00:18:31.913 --> 00:18:34.832
- Nobody's home! Leave
a message at the beep.

00:18:34.833 --> 00:18:36.041
Beep!

00:18:36.042 --> 00:18:37.751
- Open up or we'll carol!

00:18:37.752 --> 00:18:40.921
Uh, Bender!
We have company!

00:18:40.922 --> 00:18:43.799
Uh, just a
sec! I'm tidying up.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:48.555
Hii-yah!

00:18:48.930 --> 00:18:52.099
- Come in, come in!
Everything's normal.

00:18:53.268 --> 00:18:55.144
- Merry Xmas, you guys.

00:18:55.145 --> 00:18:57.688
- We didn't know you hadn't
been invited anywhere.

00:18:57.689 --> 00:19:00.733
- We came as soon as we
realized what losers you are.

00:19:00.734 --> 00:19:03.402
- Uh, punch?

00:19:03.403 --> 00:19:05.864
- Nah, I'll just have a beer.

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:11.744
- Who's hungry? We all brought

00:19:11.745 --> 00:19:14.289
our families' unique
holiday dishes.

00:19:14.998 --> 00:19:17.042
- Turducken!
- Turdolphin!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:18.500
- Huh.

00:19:18.501 --> 00:19:21.712
- How thoughtful of you all to
drop this disturbing food off,

00:19:21.713 --> 00:19:24.423
and then be immediately
on your way. Goodbye!

00:19:24.424 --> 00:19:25.966
- Dinner's served!

00:19:25.967 --> 00:19:29.178
Isn't that pretty? It
looks like a magazine.

00:19:29.179 --> 00:19:32.348
- Bender, since when
do you have three legs?

00:19:32.349 --> 00:19:34.558
- Uh, uh, th-this one's a spare.

00:19:34.559 --> 00:19:36.769
In case I break
down on the highway.

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:39.772
- And why is it
wearing a snow boot?

00:19:54.955 --> 00:19:57.706
- Finally, an
old-time happy Xmas,

00:19:57.707 --> 00:19:59.541
with presents for everyone!

00:19:59.542 --> 00:20:01.794
I'm hoping
for Batman underpants.

00:20:01.795 --> 00:20:04.380
- Santa should be
here any minute now.

00:20:06.466 --> 00:20:08.467
- The guilt is too
much! I confess!

00:20:08.468 --> 00:20:10.010
Santa won't...

00:20:11.721 --> 00:20:13.597
- What's that? Who's jingling!?

00:20:13.598 --> 00:20:16.475
- Ah, here he comes!

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.774
- Yay! It's good Santa!

00:20:23.775 --> 00:20:26.694
- Indeed, because I fixed him.

00:20:26.695 --> 00:20:29.113
- Santa seems less
dead than we thought.

00:20:30.782 --> 00:20:32.449
Ooh...

00:20:36.121 --> 00:20:38.956
I don't understand. He's still evil!

00:20:38.957 --> 00:20:41.083
I personally went back in time

00:20:41.084 --> 00:20:43.877
and reversed his
naughty-nice sensor!

00:20:43.878 --> 00:20:46.422
Uh-oh.
- What you do, old man?

00:20:46.423 --> 00:20:49.925
Oh, I've made a complete Fry of myself.

00:20:49.926 --> 00:20:53.053
You see, Santa's sensor
was exactly like the one

00:20:53.054 --> 00:20:54.638
on this punch bowl.

00:20:54.639 --> 00:20:56.181
When he was first built,

00:20:56.182 --> 00:20:58.601
it was in the correct position.

00:20:58.602 --> 00:21:02.021
But when I went back in
time, I flipped it around.

00:21:02.022 --> 00:21:05.190
Me! Oh, lordy-loo.

00:21:05.191 --> 00:21:08.319
I'm the one who made Santa evil.

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:10.195
You monster!

00:21:14.576 --> 00:21:17.161
You've all
been very naughty!

00:21:17.162 --> 00:21:20.080
Especially you, Mandy.

00:21:20.081 --> 00:21:23.542
- I'm sorry I forgot
to feed the hamster!

00:21:23.543 --> 00:21:25.419
- Arm yourselves!

00:21:35.221 --> 00:21:37.389
Cookie?

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:41.810
- And here we are, last Xmas.

00:21:41.811 --> 00:21:43.354
Get him!

00:21:43.355 --> 00:21:46.273
- Bite my glittering
festive ass.

00:21:47.734 --> 00:21:51.695
Unhand me, you
naughty boys.

00:21:51.696 --> 00:21:53.614
Who are those handsome guys,

00:21:53.615 --> 00:21:55.449
and what are they
doing to poor Santa?

00:21:55.450 --> 00:21:57.576
- That's us, you idiot.

00:21:57.577 --> 00:21:59.787
You didn't take us to last Xmas.

00:21:59.788 --> 00:22:03.207
You took us to next
Xmas! Meaning this Xmas!

00:22:03.208 --> 00:22:05.459
- Damn it, Bender. I'm a doctor,

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.086
not a time machine guy!

00:22:13.051 --> 00:22:15.636
I think I speak for everyone when I say,

00:22:15.637 --> 00:22:17.179
uh-whuh?

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:19.014
- I can't hold it in anymore!

00:22:20.433 --> 00:22:23.477
- We kidnapped and
murdered Santa!

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:28.524
- Oh.
- We didn't mean to, but still!

00:22:30.318 --> 00:22:32.945
- Stop blubbering, you bloobs!

00:22:32.946 --> 00:22:34.405
You're heroes!

00:22:34.406 --> 00:22:36.031
What-roes?

00:22:36.032 --> 00:22:38.284
- The professor
set Santa to kill!

00:22:38.285 --> 00:22:41.328
You saved all
19 of us!

00:22:41.329 --> 00:22:44.081
- We're heroes?
- Damn right, we are!

00:22:44.082 --> 00:22:47.418
Do the Bender! Do
the Bender! Do the Bender!

00:22:47.419 --> 00:22:49.253
Aw, Bender!

00:22:49.254 --> 00:22:51.297
You and Zoidberg
are friends now?

00:22:51.298 --> 00:22:52.756
That's so cute.

00:22:52.757 --> 00:22:54.717
- Uh, absolutely not!

00:22:54.718 --> 00:22:56.885
You're all having a
mass hallucination!

00:22:56.886 --> 00:22:59.805
- So, what happened to Santa?

00:23:00.890 --> 00:23:02.474
- You're drinking out of him.

00:23:02.475 --> 00:23:04.893
- There's one thing I
still don't understand.

00:23:04.894 --> 00:23:07.438
Which one of you meatbags
wrote the creepy notes?

00:23:09.232 --> 00:23:10.941
'Twas I!

00:23:14.821 --> 00:23:17.072
I sent the notes
from the future!

00:23:17.073 --> 00:23:18.616
- Because I murdered you?

00:23:18.617 --> 00:23:22.453
- No! Because I knew
what you did next Xmas.

00:23:22.454 --> 00:23:24.913
You became friends
with Zoidberg!

00:23:24.914 --> 00:23:26.999
So I'm blackmailing you!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:30.169
- No... No!

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:31.670
You take Amy's Venmo?

00:23:31.671 --> 00:23:33.297
- Sure.
- Hey!

00:23:37.677 --> 00:23:38.928
Cookie!

00:23:42.015 --> 00:23:43.390
- Yo, Santa Bot!

00:23:43.391 --> 00:23:47.311
I'ma drop my Futurama
Xmas list for 3023.

00:23:47.312 --> 00:23:50.272
Y'all ready for this?
I'm about to get nice.

00:23:51.274 --> 00:23:53.068
Kwanzaabot. Yeah.